! Meme Skill

[[meme.md|../meme.md]] holds the law.
This skill carries the working procedure.


<<~ ahu #/load-contract>>

!! Load Contract

Keep these points active when the skill loads:

* the parent invariant binds the copy-shape
* memetic-wikitext, loci, invariant, and subtype laws stay distinct
* `#meta` should appear early and carry the canonical rating cluster
* the six-glyph phase map stays visible even when deeper phase sections stay absent
* `loulou` and other named `pranala` sugar should signal real outward pressure, not decorative motion
* the smallest lawful intervention beats a grand rewrite

<<~/ahu>>

<<~ ahu #/workflow-contract>>

!! Workflow Contract

Use this skill to:

# draft a new meme from the lawful copy-shape
# audit an existing meme for conformance drift
# compress an overloaded parent toward invariant form
# split examples, research, or procedure into outward surfaces

Working order:

# read the carrier fully
# detect required shape first
# classify optional depth separately
# identify which outward type laws the carrier really satisfies
# tighten the parent before creating companion memes
# verify that the result still reads as one coherent meme

Do not:

* widen the parent with archive commentary
* hide missing required structure behind pretty prose
* treat a phase stub as filled content
* award canon posture because the file sounds confident
* spray outward links that carry no actual pressure

<<~/ahu>>

<<~ ahu #/trigger>>

!! Trigger

Use this skill when the request asks to:

* create or revise a meme-law surface
* audit required versus optional structure
* build a copy-ready meme skeleton
* judge structural rating from noise through kapu
* separate meme law from subtype law or docs residue

Prefer another surface when the work concerns only:

* stable-address coherence under `loci`
* authoring-surface semantics under `memetic-wikitext`
* one subtype law with no meme-shape pressure

<<~/ahu>>

<<~ ahu #/ooda-ha>>

✶ read the carrier in document order and observe what shape actually lands on the page
⏿ sort required shape from optional depth without collapsing subtype law into meme law
◇ choose the smallest lawful shape and the highest honest posture the carrier actually earns
▶ write the lightest useful change and split skeleton, subtype, or docs matter outward as needed
↺ verify the thresholds still hold and outward claims stay truthful; name the remaining residue plainly, including what still lacks a lawful downstream home

<<~/ahu>>

<<~ ahu #/observe>>

!! ✶ Observe

Read the carrier before changing it.

Look for:

* doctype and opener
* `#meta` payload and rating cluster
* title and opening scope sentence
* body thresholds
* six-glyph phase map
* edges block
* return throat
* full phase sections, subloops, examples, or research notes
* outward composition claims in the `#has` edges

Preserve the difference between absent, stubbed, and filled surfaces.

<<~/ahu>>

<<~ ahu #/orient>>

!! ⏿ Orient

Sort findings into these buckets:

* `required-shape`
* `optional-depth`
* `subtype-law`
* `procedure-or-skeleton`
* `research-or-docs-residue`

Orientation rule:

* `required-shape` stays nearest the parent
* `optional-depth` stays only if it sharpens the invariant
* `subtype-law` usually moves to the relevant outward law
* `procedure-or-skeleton` belongs in this skill
* `research-or-docs-residue` belongs in docs

<<~/ahu>>

<<~ ahu #/decide>>

!! ◇ Decide

Choose the smallest lawful shape:

* parent only, when copy-shape pressure already reads clearly
* parent + `SKILL.md`, when drafting or audit workflow needs room
* parent + docs, when examples, tables, or research crowd the root
* parent + `SKILL.md` + docs, when law, procedure, and explanation all need different rooms

Then choose one honest structural rating:

* noise
* data
* meme
* ano
* kapu

Do not round up.

<<~/ahu>>

<<~ ahu #/act>>

!! ▶ Act

When writing or revising:

* keep the parent compact
* keep required structure visible early
* keep one-line law statements crisp
* move skeleton blocks into this skill or docs
* move large rating tables and research outward
* keep the `#has` edges truthful to the carrier actually on the page
* add `loulou` links so the split surfaces form one system

